        },
        "quote": "(a) Section C103, CONSTRUCTION DOCUMENTS, is hereby amended to include Section C103.6.4, Code footprint, which reads as follows:",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:0#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 14.85.060 block 1",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "38a56dd7-ab75-51ff-becf-1ce0feaab344",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 519,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:1",
          "start": 129
        },
        "quote": "(1) A code footprint shall be included with each set of construction documents submitted for commercial building permit review and approval. A code footprint shall mean a building and life safety code compliance document that contains both graphic and narrative information and that meets the requirements of this code section and the code official’s policy regarding format and regulation.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 14.85.060 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "b89b2793-2601-5cbd-8be8-fc9f70b43f08",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 614,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:2",
          "start": 520
        },
        "quote": "(2) Each code footprint shall be prepared by an architect registered with the State of Kansas.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 14.85.060 block 3",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 3,
          "component_id": "c0ceb95f-5344-578e-b586-111a6a64809a",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 847,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:3",
          "start": 615
        },
        "quote": "(3) A code footprint shall be prepared for all new buildings, new building additions, changes in occupancy, or building renovation, with the exception of buildings used solely as dwelling houses containing no more than two families.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:3#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 14.85.060 block 4",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 4,
          "component_id": "572c81bf-0401-5c6e-8a4d-cdadd52a4b77",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 956,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:4",
          "start": 848
        },
        "quote": "(4) All commercial projects shall be submitted with Comcheck that reflects the adopted sections of the IECC.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.85.060:block:4#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
